Suppose that $G$ satisfies
the nine CH conditions, and let $G'=[K';S']$ have logical rows $K_i'\in K_i+\mathcal C_2$ and
stabilizer rows in $\mathcal C_2$. Then $G'$ satisfies the nine CH conditions. If moreover the
rows of $S'$ span $\mathcal C_2$, then $G'$ and $G$ generate the same codes, and hence the same $n$,
$s$, $k$, and $d_Z$.
\par\hangindent 40\p@[(b)] \emph{Row basis.} Let the rows of $S$ indexed by an ordered set $I$ form a
basis of $\mathcal C_2$, and let $S_I$ be the $s\times n$ matrix they form. Restricting a syndrome
$\beta$ to its entries in $I$ gives the corresponding column $\beta_I\in\mathbb{F}_2^s$ of $S_I$.
The restriction preserves distinct and nonzero syndromes, and the columns $\beta_I$
span $\mathbb{F}_2^s$. Thus $S_I$ has the same actual rank as $S$ and is projective with $n$ columns
whenever $S$ is projective.
\par\hangindent 40\p@[(c)] \emph{Puncturing.} Let $\mathcal C'$ be the code obtained by puncturing the
set of coordinates $J$ from a code $\mathcal C\subseteq\mathbb{F}_2^n$. Deleting the columns indexed by
$J$ from a matrix whose rows span $\mathcal C$ gives a matrix whose rows span $\mathcal C'$, and
\begin{equation}\label{eq:exp-puncture-rank}
\dim\mathcal C-\dim\mathcal C'
=\dim\{\,c\in\mathcal C:{\rm supp}(c)\subseteq J\,\}
\le \lvert J\rvert.
\end{equation}
Write $\iota_J\colon\mathbb{F}_2^{n-|J|}\to\mathbb{F}_2^n$ for insertion of zeros
at each coordinate in $J$. Then $\iota_J(\mathcal C'^\perp)\subseteq\mathcal C^\perp$ and
$|\iota_Jv'|=|v'|$. Consequently, a generator matrix punctured on $J$ has $Z$-distance at least
$d_Z$ of the original.

