\label{lem:exp-projred}
Let $G=[K;S]$ satisfy the nine CH conditions with $k=3$ and $d_Z\ge3$.
If $\mathcal C_2$ is non-projective, then $S$ has a zero column $j$ or two equal columns $j\ne j'$.
In the zero-column case, form $G'$ by deleting column $j$.
In the repeated-column case, form $G'$ by deleting both equal columns $j$ and $j'$.
In either case, $G'$ satisfies:
\begin{enumerate}
\renewcommand{(\roman{enumi})}{(\roman{enumi})}
\par\hangindent 40\p@ $G'$ satisfies the nine CH conditions,
\par\hangindent 40\p@ $k'=k$,
\par\hangindent 40\p@ $d_Z(G')\ge d_Z(G)$.
